  "question": {
    "text": "If the distance between object and its two times magnified virtual image produced by a curved mirror is 15 cm , the focal length of the mirror must be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uBM3J",
      "text": "$\\frac{10}{3} \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MxgXO",
      "text": "$-12 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vQ0Gy",
      "text": "$-10 \\mathrm{~cm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "kN6YT",
      "text": "15 cm",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, image is magnified. So, it is a concave mirror.\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{m}=2=\\frac{-\\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{u}}$\n$2=\\frac{-(15-u)}{-u}$\n$2 u=15-u$\n$3 \\mathrm{u}=15 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{u}=5 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n$\\mathrm{v}=15-\\mathrm{u}=15-5=10 \\mathrm{~cm}$\nBymirror formula,\n$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{v}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{u}}$\n$=\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{1}{(-5)}=\\frac{1-2}{10}=\\frac{-1}{10}$\n$\\mathrm{f}=-10 \\mathrm{~cm}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/FMbhPp1ipYEEuzeZmymNO3AKFKp_64mssvs6hDpV_Mk.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
